§ `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`

-- Two periods in years (the ten years of Article 17(1)(a) and the fifteen years of Article 20(5)) are counted by the same three readings,
-- so the two fork points share this enumeration; each is its own field of the record, so that the two can be read differently.
-- src:444 | (a) must retain the information registered in respect of that entity for 10 years; and
-- src:528 | (5) A disqualification order is to be for such period, not exceeding 15 years, as the court directs.
@ref Article 17(1)(a) (src:444) and Article 20(5) (src:528)
DECLARE `How a number of years is counted from a day` IS ONE OF
    `the last day is the anniversary, and 29 February falls back to 28 February`
    `the last day is the anniversary, and 29 February rolls to 1 March`
    `the last day is the day before the anniversary`

-- F6.1: an application to deregister where the entity has not provided what Article 15(2) requires.
-- src:431 | (2) An entity applying for deregistration must provide the Commissioner with any information or document requested by the Commissioner in relation to the entity’s proposals for the continuation or winding up of the entity and for the application of any of its property remaining after deregistration.
-- src:432 | (3) If the entity complies with paragraph (2) the Commissioner must –
-- src:433 | (a) deregister the entity; or
-- src:434 | (b) refuse to deregister the entity on grounds relating to the proposals mentioned in paragraph (2).
