        `how long the bar on assigning the registered number lasts` IS `the bar on assigning the registered number has no end`
        `which governors Article 18(2) binds` IS `only the governors of unincorporated bodies within Article 2(1)(i)`
        `what the reasonable time of Article 18(4)(d)(ii) qualifies` IS `the reasonable time qualifies only the failure to take proper steps`
        `whether a disqualification that has ended is a reportable matter` IS `a disqualification counts although it has ended`
        `when the ban of Article 19(10) starts` IS `the ban starts on the report to the Commissioner`
        `whether acting in breach of Article 19(2) or (4) is an offence` IS `Article 19(11) reaches only paragraph (10)`
        `how a report is judged prompt under Article 19(2)` IS `promptness is a determination supplied as an input`
        `whether the time for objections must be reasonable` IS `the time specified must be reasonable or the deregistration is not authorised`
        `how the fifteen years of Article 20(5) are counted` IS `the last day is the anniversary, and 29 February falls back to 28 February`
        `how the duty in Article 19(9)(e)(i) stands against Article 28(3)` IS `Article 28(3) prevails and no duty to require removal arises for an organized religious charity`
        `how a term of imprisonment of one year or two years is measured` IS `calendar months`
        `when the Commissioner may deregister after giving the preliminary notice` IS `the Commissioner may deregister only after the last day for objections`
        `how the ten years of Article 17(1)(a) are counted` IS `the last day is the anniversary, and 29 February falls back to 28 February`
        `when the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` IS `the notice has not been complied with once the time it names has ended without the steps taken`
        `whether a declaration given on the day of the application is in time` IS `a declaration given on the day of the application is in time`
        `from when a governor who has been notified is in breach of Article 19(4)` IS reading
        `whether the last day named in a time limit is inside the permission` IS `the day named is the last day of the permission`
        `whose view of expediency lets a person apply under Article 20(3)` IS `only the applicant's own view that it is expedient`
        `whether assisting another governor is misconduct only if that governor engages in misconduct` IS `the assisting or encouraging is misconduct only if the other governor engages in misconduct`

